From 735387878abfbf7f74df2099676aa594d5a2b861 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NEXUS <nexus@localhost>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 23:03:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 14/22] nexus_engine 0.4: per-game save folders, reliable NEXUS
 Home, F11, screenshots, controller choice, reveal after the loading screen

- savedata_factory: NexusSaveFolders() maps a game's account/device save to folders NEXUS names
  in the save directory (request "saveFolders"); empty table = upstream layout; test case
- Home: the Guide/Home and capture buttons are removed from the game's controls (they reached
  the emulated HOME button through input_common's SDL event watch and opened the game's
  return-to-HOME handling); one press = one request (500 ms, not while suspended or right after
  a resume)
- F11 (fullscreenKey) toggles fullscreen/windowed without stopping the game; windowed at 16:9,
  80% of the display it is on
- F12 (screenshotKey) and the controller capture/share button save a PNG with a unique name in
  screenshotDir
- controllers: players mapped to the controllers NEXUS chose (guid/port); nexus_engine_controllers
  lists connected controllers (name, type, vendor/product, serial)
- revealOnRequest / nexus_engine_reveal: after the first frame the window waits for NEXUS to fade
  its loading screen out (failsafe timeout); optional fadeInMs opacity fade
- status: ready, fullscreen, screenshots, lastScreenshot

(cherry picked from commit 14005c17116b2826c1da94f619275c3c12520bf8)
